 "recap": [
  "Ligatures join two words when one modifies the other: -ng after a vowel, -g after n, na after any other consonant.",
  "The ligature goes after the first word, and the order can be swapped without changing the meaning.",
  "Many sequences take ligatures: noun + noun, verb + adverb, adjective + adjective for emphasis, and more.",
  "Exceptions: kung; a possessive pronoun after a noun (aklát ko); an adjective + ka or kayó (Marúnong ka).",
  "With several adjectives, only the last takes the ligature."
